# A structure member passed to a function's VAR_IN_OUT.
#
# Derivation: a VAR_IN_OUT parameter refers to the caller's variable, which
# the function reads and writes (ed.3 6.6.2.3, 6.6.1.7.1 table 20; ed.2
# 2.5.1.3). A member of a structured variable, and a member of an element of
# an array of structures, are variables (ed.3 6.4.4.2, 6.4.4.3, 7.3.1; ed.2
# 2.4.1.2). p and pa are the program's VAR, initially 0 (ed.3 table 10) and
# retained between cycles. BUMP adds d to the member and returns its new
# value.
#   cycle 0, i=1: p.x = 0+5 = 5;   pa[1].x = 0+1 = 1  -> r1 5  r2 1, e 1 0 0
#   cycle 1, i=3: p.x = 10;        pa[3].x = 1        -> r1 10 r2 1, e 1 0 1
#   cycle 2, i=1: p.x = 15;        pa[1].x = 2        -> r1 15 r2 2, e 2 0 1
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: i
outputs: r1 r2 px e1 e2 e3
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.2.3, 6.6.1.7.1 (table 20), 6.4.4.2, 7.3.1
---
0 i=1 => r1=5 r2=1 px=5 e1=1 e2=0 e3=0
1 i=3 => r1=10 r2=1 px=10 e1=1 e2=0 e3=1
2 i=1 => r1=15 r2=2 px=15 e1=2 e2=0 e3=1
